julia: `engine = "julia"` can marshal `phylo()` only for univariate Gaussian,
Poisson, NB2, Gamma, Beta, Binomial, or bivariate Gaussian (q=4) fits.
ℹ Use native `engine = "tmb"` for other phylogenetic fits until the bridge has
  parity tests. 

### CELL D2: relmat() on mu1
julia: `engine = "julia"` routes `relmat()` / `animal()` / `spatial()`
structured terms only for univariate Gaussian, Poisson, NB2, or Gamma fits.
ℹ DRM.jl fits these general-covariance random intercepts for those families;
  use `engine = "tmb"` for "biv_student" structured models. 

